{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mq9oyqtm4kt","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Inline main-agent work traps as catch-all waste — fix is a taskTranscript main-session fallback","summary":"ROOT CAUSE of trapped_tokens from inline work: when the MAIN agent claims a task and works INLINE in its driving-session transcript, no SubagentStart hook fires, so the assignee agent record has no transcript_path and no session. daemon.js taskTranscript() (lines ~963-983) falls through all resolution steps and returns null, so the task's tokens are never split to the claim — they stay in the session catch-all node (own = total - claimed) and, with no merged output, are counted as trapped_tokens (the very metric task .../4 minimizes). FIX (read-side only, zero protocol change): the main-session id equals basename(mainTranscript,'.jsonl'); add a step in taskTranscript that, when the task's `session` equals it, resolves to st.mainTranscript directly. Safe even when multiple tasks share the main session because splitSessionTokens divides the shared total honestly by claim-window duration (same mechanism that already covers shared subagent transcripts). Add pure helper isMainSession(session, mainTranscript). Mirrors the prior token-linkage fix (6e9b897c/12) which resolved SUBAGENT transcripts; this closes the symmetric MAIN-agent gap. NOTE: this worker session has Bash/Write/Edit permission-denied AND orch-gate blocks orchestrator-source edits (gate keys on harness session_id f2a0c314, which has no graph claim), so the patch could not be landed from here — must be applied by a session with ORCH_GATE_OFF=1 or a .off marker.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-11T16:07:58.282Z","vec":[-0.12763753533363342,0.0054208398796617985,0.005789473187178373,-0.004317029379308224,0.05884997546672821,0.009653083048760891,0.022929051890969276,0.0548359677195549,0.023294368758797646,0.0684773400425911,-0.047386255115270615,-0.022145766764879227,0.0043881600722670555,0.0181508976